    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n188" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">abruptĭo</span></b> , ōnis,
			f.
		abrumpo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a breaking</i> or <i>tearing off</i>, <i>a rending asunder.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: corrigiae, <i>of a
				shoe-latchet</i>, * <i><span class="en">Cic. Div.
				2, 40, 84</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: augurii, <i>interruption</i>, Paul. ex Fest. pp. 270 and 271 Müll.
			—Of divorce, Att. ap. <i><span class="en">Cic. Att.
				11, 3, 1</span></i>.</div>
